------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Change Log  (only recent)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unreleased
	Fixes for issues #94 to #99, #102, #107, #141 to #144 and #195,
	and for defects found while fixing them.
	Values and row names that change:
	  rbp sets the range of its gains before using it, so its value
	    no longer depends on the build or on -q (#94).
	  Under -c, num_rel on the all row counts only judgments at or
	    above -l, and only in the topic that -D names (#95).
	  Under -c, a qrels topic missing from the run is evaluated as a
	    ranking that retrieves nothing, not as a placeholder
	    document. utility, rbp_resid and relstring with parameters,
	    and gain maps that give level -1 a gain, change for such a
	    topic; utility gives p3 * num_rel + p4 * (N - num_rel),
	    where N is the -N value (#96).
	  A topic whose grades are all negative is evaluated with its
	    own grade counts, instead of exiting 4, crashing or using
	    the previous topic's ideal ranking (#97).
	  Gain maps whose gains differ by less than 1 are sorted
	    correctly, which changes ndcg, ideal_dcg, Rndcg, ndcg_rel
	    and G for such maps (#98).
	  ndcg_rel and Rndcg give 0 instead of inf or nan when no ideal
	    gain is positive (#98, #142 item 9).
	  dcg, ideal_dcg and ndcg each keep their own gain map, so two
	    of them with gain maps no longer crash or mix their gains
	    and names (#195).
	  11pt_avg sorts its recall levels (#142 item 5). 11pt_avg and
	    iprec_at_recall give 0 instead of nan for a topic that
	    retrieves nothing, as under -J or -M 0 (#142 item 4).
	  Integer cutoffs that differ by 2^31 or more are sorted
	    correctly (#142 item 12).
	  -Z uses only the zscores line of the same topic and measure,
	    and a missing line gives -1000000 (#144 item 1).
	  With no -m, -R qrels_jg, prefs and qrels_prefs print their own
	    default measures instead of exiting 4 (#141 item 1).
	  bpref and gm_bpref with a very large -l give 0 instead of
	    crashing (#102).
	  relstring with a length beyond the ranking lists the whole
	    ranking on every build (#142 item 2).
	  Rprec_mult and Rprec_mult_avgjg print each multiple to two
	    decimals in the row name, without truncation (#142 item 14).
	Inputs refused with exit status 2:
	  A run score with no leading number, or NaN (#107).
	  A qrels or qrels_jg level outside -127 to 127, and a prefs or
	    qrels_prefs level that is not a number (#143 items 3 and 4).
	  A NUL byte, or a CR that ends neither a line nor the file, in
	    any input (#143 items 1, 5, 7 and 10).
	  A judgments file (qrels, qrels_jg, prefs or qrels_prefs) with
	    no data lines, and a results file or standard input with
	    only comments or blank lines, which crashed (#99,
	    #143 item 2).
	  A zscores mean or standard deviation that is not finite, and a
	    negative standard deviation (#143 item 12). An unusable
	    zscores file exits 2 instead of 255 (#141 item 4).
	  Measure parameters that cannot be used: a gain name that is
	    not a relevance level or repeats one, an rbp p given twice,
	    a value that is not a finite number, a recall level outside
	    [0, 1], a multiple of R not above 0, a negative set_F
	    weight, an rbp p outside [0, 1), cutoffs that print the same
	    row name, and utility without four coefficients. Some of
	    these exited 4 at the first topic
	    (#142 items 6 to 8, 11, 15 and 16).
	Options refused with exit status 1:
	  A negative -l, -M or -N (#142 items 1, 10 and 13).
	Inputs refused with exit status 4:
	  Where long has 32 bits, as on Windows, an input whose table of
	    counts would not fit in a long, such as a prefs judgment
	    group of 65,536 documents (#143 item 9).
	Inputs read differently:
	  A run score, prefs level, zscores value or measure parameter
	    with characters after the number is read with a warning, and
	    a run score beyond the range of a double is kept as inf or 0
	    with a warning (#107, #142 item 7, #143 items 3, 12, 13).
	  In a judgments file, a line whose first non-blank character is
	    # is a comment wherever it is, and a blank line is skipped
	    with a warning (#143 items 2 and 8).
	  A UTF-8 byte-order mark is skipped (#143 item 6).
	  Only "-" reads results from standard input (#143 item 11).
	  Standard input is read in full and checked as a file is
	    (#143 item 10).
	  On 64-bit builds, judgments and zscores files of 2 GiB or more
	    are read in full (#143 item 9).
	Messages and help:
	  Without -c, a qrels topic missing from the run gives "qrels
	    qid '<qid>' not found in results" before any output
	    (#141 items 2 and 3).
	  Messages name their file, line and source, use the prefix of
	    the file that prints them, and end with a newline;
	    "Malformed line" counts comment and blank lines
	    (#141 items 5 to 7, #142 item 17, #143 item 14).
	  The help corrects the -N default, the long form of -M, the -c
	    description, the default measures for each -R and the input
	    rules, and states the measure parameter limits
	    (#141 items 1, 2 and 8, #142 items 6, 10 and 11,
	    #143 items 4 and 8).
	Also fixed, without an issue:
	  A failed write to standard output gives "Can't write to
	    standard output" and exit status 8, instead of exit 0.
	  A prefs pair on which more than 65,535 judgment groups agree
	    exits 4, where its count wrapped to 0.
	  Where long has 32 bits, a topic id of 2 GiB or more exits 4.
	  The readers pass bytes above 127 to isspace and isdigit as
	    unsigned char.
	Memory and internals, with no change in printed values:
	  bpref and gm_bpref no longer read past their grade table, rbp
	    and relstring no longer leak for each topic, and utility,
	    Rprec_mult, the sorts and the rank comparators no longer
	    overflow or cut sizes and ranks to 32 bits (#102,
	    #142 items 2 and 3, #143 item 9, #144 items 2 to 4).
	  Removed clear_relstr (#144 item 3) and m_ndcg_p.c, which the
	    Makefile did not build (#141 item 9).
	  Malloc and Realloc call te_malloc_array and te_realloc_array,
	    defined in utility_pool.c, and return NULL when the size
	    does not fit in a size_t. functions.h declares the shared
	    readers, number conversions and te_comp_double; trec_eval.h
	    defines MIN_REL_LEVEL and MAX_REL_LEVEL.
	  make quicktest builds three test programs and runs the scripts
	    in test/regress. CI adds sanitizer and 32-bit builds.
6/18/26 Version 10.0
	Breaking fix: change uses of int truncation to round/floor.
	-c mode now prints out skipped queries in -q mode.
	Added measures to the all_trec set: rbp, rbp_resid, unj_5/10/20
	Support for '#' comment lines in TREC-format runs and qrels files.
       Fixes for GCC 15 and Windows
       Allow results files to be read from stdin
	Added LICENSE: MIT-ish
	Code reformatted
